--       (hb : 1 ≤ b) (hr : 1 ≤ r) (hbig : 2 * r * 2 ^ (2 * p) < 2 ^ (b - 1))
--       (s : IState HS) (f : Fin HS → List ℤ) (zx zy : List GI) (lx ly : List ℤ)
--       (hX : f vX = gflat zx ++ lx) (hY : f vY = gflat zy ++ ly) (hlx : zx.length = r)
--       (hly : zy.length = r)
--       (hzx : ∀ z ∈ zx, |z.1| ≤ 2 ^ p ∧ |z.2| ≤ 2 ^ p) (hzy : ∀ z ∈ zy, |z.1| ≤ 2 ^ p ∧ |z.2| ≤ 2 ^ p)
--       (hT : Tmp f)
--       (hP : PV (πr (2 ^ p) (NLogN.KFV.kG b r (2 ^ p)) b r ((2 ^ b) ^ (2 * r)) (2 ^ Δ)) s)
--       (hF : PZ (πr (2 ^ p) (NLogN.KFV.kG b r (2 ^ p)) b r ((2 ^ b) ^ (2 * r)) (2 ^ Δ)) f) :
--       IRuns I iprog (recU pM) (encK s f)
--         (encK s (Function.update (Function.update (Function.update f vX lx) vY ly) vO
--           ((gflat (kmulD r Δ zx zy)).reverse ++ f vO)))
--         (2000 * cRec r p b Δ φ)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B3 (chunk kernel), part 0: one uniform Kronecker record product with general truncation
--
--   `KFV10Rec.recU_runs` with the truncation `Δ` free (there `Δ = p + ρ`; the program `recU` reads
--   `2^Δ` from the parameter stack `kD`): on records `zx, zy` of length `r` (entries `|·| ≤ 2^p`,
--   digit width `b` with `2 r 2^{2p} < 2^{b-1}`), `recU` leaves the reversed record
--   `kmulD r Δ zx zy`, entry `j` = the `y^r + 1`-folded numerators truncated by `2^Δ`.
--   With `Δ = 0` and zero-padded records this is the exact Gaussian polynomial product
--   (the Toeplitz stages of the chunk kernel).
